            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="0313" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./90</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the American Member of the Inter-American Neutrality
                        Committee</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fenwick</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-04-30">April 30, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Professor Fenwick</hi>: I have received your
                    telegram of April 29th in which you tell me that the Committee’s recommendation
                    on the security zone has been completed. I note that, while the recommendation
                    strongly defends the principle of the zone, it leaves the question of measures
                    of enforcement subject to investigation by a special committee and to subsequent
                    consultation between Foreign Ministers of the American Republics.</p>
                <p>This procedure appears to me satisfactory as far as it goes; I hope that the
                    recommendation will, however, include a discussion of the measures which the
                    American Republics might adopt and of the lines of investigation in regard
                    thereto which your Committee believes should be pursued by the proposed special
                    committee.</p>
                <p>It is my opinion that, for the time being at least, it would not be desirable to
                    give publicity to your recommendations on this subject. …</p>
                <p>I have very much appreciated your courtesy in keeping me informed of the progress
                    of your Committee’s deliberations. With cordial regards,</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
